for editorial warmth and visual hierarchy; notch
for mechanical precision on tags; and superellipse()
for fine control between round
and squircle
. And the ability to mix values per corner (round bevel bevel round
, scoop round
) opens up shapes that would have required SVG masks or clip-path
hacks.
We went from five background images to border-radius
, to corner-shape
. Each step removed a category of workarounds. I’m excited to see what designers do with this one.
